  ⟦fg=#94e2d5 bold⟧▎ Steps⟦/⟧

  ⟦fg=#89b4fa⟧1.⟦/⟧ ⟦bold⟧Compute the discriminant⟦/⟧
     ⟦fg=#f38ba8 ul=curly ulc=#f38ba8⟧\Delta = b^2 - 4ac⟦/⟧.
  ⟦fg=#89b4fa⟧2.⟦/⟧ ⟦bold⟧Check its sign⟦/⟧:
     ⟦fg=#89b4fa⟧◦⟦/⟧ If ⟦fg=#f38ba8 ul=curly ulc=#f38ba8⟧\Delta > 0⟦/⟧: two real roots.
     ⟦fg=#89b4fa⟧◦⟦/⟧ If ⟦fg=#f38ba8 ul=curly ulc=#f38ba8⟧\Delta = 0⟦/⟧: one real root.
     ⟦fg=#89b4fa⟧◦⟦/⟧ If ⟦fg=#f38ba8 ul=curly ulc=#f38ba8⟧\Delta < 0⟦/⟧: two complex
       roots.
  ⟦fg=#89b4fa⟧3.⟦/⟧ ⟦bold⟧Apply the formula⟦/⟧ above.

  ⟦fg=#6c7086⟧▎⟦/⟧ ⟦fg=#a6adc8 bold⟧Note:⟦/⟧⟦fg=#a6adc8⟧ when ⟦/⟧⟦fg=#f38ba8 ul=curly ulc=#f38ba8⟧a = 0⟦/⟧⟦fg=#a6adc8⟧ the equation is⟦/⟧
  ⟦fg=#6c7086⟧▎⟦/⟧ ⟦fg=#a6adc8⟧linear, not quadratic.⟦/⟧

